  "interpretation": "The hole behind an emptied touch is a level-memory structure, not a placement geometry: on the tape an emptied price stays empty for tens to hundreds of events (median delay + p_never are the headline stats) and is usually re-occupied as the new touch by an improving submission, while sim arms re-occupy levels almost immediately (or never, when the level can only be reached inside the spread). Placement-law and inner-edge knobs cannot express this \u2014 the missing mechanism is a per-price refill timescale.",
